# Vauxhall 30-98, 1913-1927.
#
# Britain's first great sporting car: 4,318 mm long, 1,727 mm wide, 1,524 mm high,
# 2,972 mm wheelbase; 4,224 cc four, overhead valves, capable of about 130 km/h.
# About 600 built. Chosen as a photographed substitute for the unverifiable
# "Daimler 38 hp" entry in the section F table.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vauxhall_30-98
#
# Colours: Black, British Racing Green, Maroon and Grey are documented period
# finishes.
#
# Weight: 12 in total (black 5, green 3, maroon 2, grey 2).
#
# Speed 130 km/h; comfort 65/280 (line). Class 4.
# Dates: 1913-1927 with a road tail to about 1948.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-30-98.blend. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-30-98/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
